hadiths[48]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3698","Daylami (the narrator is doubtful or perhaps Ibn Daylami) narrates: I accepted Islam and I had two sisters in my marriage."
"3699","Dahhak bin Firoz Daylami narrates this statement of his father: When I accepted Islam, I had two sisters in marriage, I inquired about this from the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he instructed me: I should divorce one of them."
"3700","Uza'i was asked about a Harbi man who is the husband of two sisters, and he said, \If it were not for the hadith in which it is narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave authority to the husband in such a case"," I would have given this fatwa"," that man (will live with the woman to whom he was previously married).\"""""
"3701","Imam Shafi'i says: When a person is a Muslim and his wives are full sisters, then that person can choose one of them whom he wants, then his marriage with that woman will remain intact, his marriage with the other woman will be annulled, it does not make a difference in this regard (before accepting Islam) whether he married them both together or one after the other."
"3702","Sayyidna Sahl bin Saad Sa’idi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: An Ansari man came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is your opinion about a person who finds a person with his wife, if he kills that woman, then you will kill him. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Allah has given a decision about you and your wife. The narrator narrates: These two husband and wife cursed in the mosque, I was there along with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the narrator says. The narrator says that the woman was pregnant, the man denied her pregnancy, then the woman's son was called after his mother, after that it was customary that such a woman became the heir of her child, and that child became the heir of that woman, the Juwala appointed as the inheritance of the son."
"3703","Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: An Ansari from Banuzriq accused his wife of adultery, he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned him back four times, then God revealed the verses regarding the order of cursing, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Where is the questioner? A great order was revealed by Allah, then the man insisted on cursing and the woman also decided that she would remove the punishment from herself. Another person will have children. (The narrator narrates) So this woman gave birth to a black child, which was like a beige (i.e. dark-colored) camel, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called this child, and entrusted him to his mother's relatives."
"3704","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Saad Sa’idi (RA) narrates: I was present in the case of the one who cursed (husband and wife) in front of the Prophet (PBUH). This man divorced the woman three times in the presence of the Prophet (PBUH) and the Prophet declared them valid. After that, the same Sunnah was practiced among those who cursed that husband and wife were separated and then they could never be together."
"3705","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa'd Sa'idi (RA) narrates: Awaimar Ajlani said to a member of his tribe: Ask the Prophet (PBUH) about a person who finds another person with his wife. Both of them cursed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated them and said that these two can never be together."
"3706","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When cursed people (husband and wife) separate from each other, they can never be together again."
"3707","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: What he said is in the next hadith) Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) (and both Sayyidna Ibn Masoud may Allah be pleased with him) say: This is the Sunnah of those who curse, that they can never be together."
"3708","Sayyidna Ali (RA) and Sayyidna Ibn Mas'ud (RA) both say: This is the prevalent Sunnah that cursers can never come together afterwards."
"3709","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Jafar (RA) narrates: I was present with the Prophet (PBUH) when the Prophet (PBUH) made a curse between Awimar Ajlani and his wife. Come, the order of the Qur'an has been revealed about both of you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed them both about this pregnancy near the pulpit after Asr prayer."
"3710","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"3711","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) was cursed with regard to pregnancy."
"3712",", Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrates: Hilal bin Umayyah accused his wife in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of having illicit relations with Sharik bin Sahma, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Produce evidence"," otherwise you will be subject to false accusations of adultery.\"" The narrator narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say this"," you must provide evidence"," otherwise the limit of falsely accusing you of adultery will continue. The narrator narrates: Hilal bin Umayyah said: By the One who sent you with the truth"," I am telling the truth and Allah will surely send down a decree about me that will not cause me to be bound. \""Those who accuse their wives: this verse is up to the fifth time she will say: Allah's wrath has descended on her. The group of men are truthful.\"" The narrator narrates: After that"," the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) summoned them both. Then the woman stood up and she also testified. When she started to use the fifth sentence"," the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""Stop it"," because it (the fifth testimony) will make punishment for her in the Hereafter.\"" Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrates: The woman hesitated"," she bowed her head until we thought that she would turn back now"," but then she said: I will never disgrace my tribe. A narrator named Hisham narrates"," I think my teacher has quoted the same words as a narrator named Muhammad"," and if this woman gave birth to a child with gray eyes"," a heavy head and strong legs"," then he will be the offspring of Sharik bin Sahma"," then this woman gave birth to such a child. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the order of the Book of Allah had not come earlier"," then my behavior with this woman would have been different."""
"3713","Qazi Shareeh narrates: Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said to me (may Allah guide him) the person in whose hand is the knot of marriage."
"3714","Yahya bin Abd al-Rahman and Abu Salama narrate: Sayyidna Jubayr bin Mut'am (may Allah be pleased with him) married a woman from Banu Nazir, and then divorced her before leaving. Sayyidna Jubayr sent her a full dowry, and said, \I have more right to forgive than that woman (because Allah says). Except if he forgives women or the person in whose hand the knot of marriage is forgiven.\"" Jubayr bin Mut'am said) I have more right to forgive than this woman."""
"3715","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"3716","Abu Salamah narrates: Sayyidna Jubayr bin Mut’im married a woman and then divorced her before leaving. He recited this verse: Except in the case that he forgives the woman or the person in whose hand the knot of marriage is forgiven."
"3717","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The person who has the marriage knot in his hand means the husband."
"3718","Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The guardian of the marriage knot means the husband."
"3719","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, says about this decree of Allah: Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, says: \Except for the case that he forgives the women.\"" Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas"," may Allah be pleased with him"," says: That is"," he forgives the woman or the person in whose hand the knot of marriage is forgiven."""
"3720","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: This means the husband."
"3721","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: This means the husband."
"3722","Muhammad bin Jubayr narrates: His father (Sayyidna Jubayr bin Mut'am, may Allah be pleased with him) married a woman and then divorced her before leaving."
"3723","Saeed bin Musayyib says: The person who has the marriage knot in his hand means the husband."
"3724","Qazi Shareeh says: This refers to the husband, that is, if he wants, he should give the woman full mahrada. Ibrahim, Alqamah and Hasan al-Basri say: It means Wali."
"3725","Qubaisa bin Dhu'ib narrates: Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (may God be pleased with him) was asked about two sisters who are owned by someone, then Sayyidna Uthman said: I will neither instruct you nor forbid you because one verse declares them halal and one verse declares them forbidden. The questioner went out and met a companion. A narrator named Muammar has narrated this: I think it was Sayyidna Ali (may God be pleased with him), he inquired about what you had asked Sayyidna Uthman about. The man told about his question and also about his answer, then Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: I will forbid you if I have any (official authority) over you and then you commit it, I will punish you."
"3726","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) was asked about this issue, if a mother and a daughter come under the ownership of a person, can one of them have intercourse with the other? So Sayyiduna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu said, I would not like you to associate with them both."
"3727","Narrated ``Urayb: I asked Sayyiduna Ali (may God be pleased with him) that a slave girl and her mother are in my possession, both of them have given birth to my children. What is your opinion about this? Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: One verse declares it halal and one verse declares it forbidden. I will not do this, nor will any member of my family do this."
"3728","Narrated Tariq Bin Qays: I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may a man have intercourse with both his maidservant and his daughter, while they both belong to him. So Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: One verse has declared both of them haram and one verse has declared them halal, but I will not do that."
"3729","Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, When a man marries a beautiful woman, he should stay with her for three days and then start dividing (among the wives)."
"3730","Narrated Anas: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that the virgin will get seven days and the Saiba will get three days, then the man will divide (the time equally between) his wives."
"3731","Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA) narrated: He said to the Prophet (PBUH): He held the foot of the Prophet (PBUH) and (said) you, the Prophet (PBUH) will stay with me today. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Saiba will get three days and the virgin will get seven days."
"3732","Abdul Malik bin Abu Bakr narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Sayyida Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with him) in the month of Shawwal, and he departed in the month of Shawwal. Sayyida Umm Salma said, O Messenger of Allah (now), you may stay with me for three days."
"3733","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission: Abd al-Malik bin Abu Bakr narrates the following statement of Sayyidah Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, regarding her father: When he left, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: You are not inferior to your husband. But then I will stay with all my wives (with each of them) for seven days, then Sayyida Umm Salma asked you to stay with me for three days. Imam Malik and Ibn Abi Zayb have derived this ruling from him that a virgin will be left for seven days and that with Saiba will be left for three days."
"3734","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: The text of the hadith is after the next chain of transmission. Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When a man marries a virgin and the man has a wife from his first wife, that virgin will get three days, and if he marries a female, she will get two days."
"3735","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: It often happened that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit all his wives. was"
"3736","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not have company, only touched."
"3737","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When you marry a free woman and your first wife is a slave woman, you should give two days to the free woman and one day to the slave woman."
"3738","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When the first wife is a concubine and then someone marries a free man, the share of the concubine will be one-third and the share of the free woman will be two-thirds."
"3739","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Sayyida Safiyya (may Allah be pleased with him) and declared her freedom as his dower."
"3740","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Sayyida Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) and married her and declared her freedom as her dowry."
"3741","Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Sayyida Safiyyah bint Hayy (may Allah be pleased with him) and married her and made her the dowry of her freedom."
"3742","Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Sayyida Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with him) and married her and declared her dowry to be her freedom."
"3743","Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) married Sayyid Safiyyah (RA). Thabit narrates: I inquired whether the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had paid her dowry. So Sayyiduna Anas said that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had paid her her dowry, and the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had freed her and married her."
"3744","Qatadah narrates: Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) was asked about a person who frees his slave girl and marries her, so he said: Did the Prophet (PBUH) not free Sayyida Safiyyah bint Hayy (RA) and Sayyida Juwayriyyah Bint Harith (RA) and marry them with their freedom as their dowry?"
"3745","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this about a person who has intercourse with his wife during her menstruation: He should give one dinar (maybe the narrator has doubts) and half a dinar in charity."
